.TH SDL_SetGPUTextureName 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetGPUTextureName \- Sets an arbitrary string constant to label a texture.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_SetGPUTextureName(
.BI "    SDL_GPUDevice *device,
.BI "    SDL_GPUTexture *texture,
.BI "    const char *text);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You should use
.BR SDL_PROP_GPU_TEXTURE_CREATE_NAME_STRING
with
.BR SDL_CreateGPUTexture
instead of this function to avoid thread safety issues\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I device
a GPU Context\[char46]
.TP
.I texture
a texture to attach the name to\[char46]
.TP
.I text
a UTF-8 string constant to mark as the name of the texture\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function is not thread safe, you must make sure the texture is not simultaneously used by any other thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateGPUTexture (3)
